# A NetComm SmartModem 2400SA calling a Cisco at 300 bit/s, recorded by
# somebody else in 2013 and published with the audio.  Nothing in it came
# out of this code, which is the whole reason it is here: the twelve
# fixtures beside it were all minted from calls modec placed, so any of
# them could in principle pass by agreeing with a mistake modec makes at
# both ends.  This one cannot.
#
# The recording is stereo with one direction per channel, and on this
# page the *answering* modem is on the left -- the opposite of the V.34
# collection the Banksia file comes from.  See
# recordings/third-party/README.md.
#
# The reference below is not modec reading itself back.  minimodem 0.24,
# pointed at this same file, returns the identical 122 bytes:
#
#     minimodem --rx -f netcomm-2400sa-bell103-300.wav \
#               --mark 2225 --space 2025 300
#
# It adds three 0xff bytes of its own at the carrier edges, which the
# byte gate here suppresses; every other byte agrees, including the
# strange ` Username: username: login: ' the far end really does send
# three times over.  So the expect: lines below are checked against an
# implementation that shares nothing with this one.
source:    recordings/third-party/netcomm-2400sa-300bps.wav, left channel
seconds:   38.0
role:      originate
modes:     bell103,v21
v8:        no
connect:   Bell103 300
expect:    User Access Verification
expect:    Username:
tolerance: 0
